TITLE:: FluidLoadStore
summary:: Save and restore the loader information of a FluidModel
categories:: Libraries>FluidModel
related:: Classes/FluidModel, Classes/FluidLoadFolder, Classes/FluidLoadMultiple

DESCRIPTION::
link::Classes/FluidModel#-store:: and link::Classes/FluidModel#-load:: use FluidLoadStore to save which files a corpus was made of and where each one sits in the joined buffer. After loading, a FluidLoadStore stands in for the original link::Classes/FluidLoadFolder:: or link::Classes/FluidLoadMultiple:: as the model's link::Classes/FluidModel#-loader::: it answers the same code::files::, code::index:: and code::buffer:: messages.

You normally do not use this class directly.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: files
An Array of sound file paths. They are opened to read their headers, so they must still exist.

ARGUMENT:: index
An index dictionary as made by link::Classes/FluidLoadFolder:: (see link::Classes/FluidLoadMultiple#-index::).

ARGUMENT:: buffer
The joined link::Classes/Buffer::.

returns:: A FluidLoadStore.

METHOD:: store
Write a loader's file list (code::loader_files_<name>.scd::), index (code::loader_index_<name>.scd::) and buffer (code::loader_buffer_<name>.aiff::) to a folder.

ARGUMENT:: loader
A link::Classes/FluidLoadFolder::, link::Classes/FluidLoadMultiple:: or FluidLoadStore.

ARGUMENT:: path
An existing folder.

ARGUMENT:: name
The name used in the file names (the model's key).

METHOD:: load
Read the files written by link::#*store::. The buffer is read from code::<name>.aiff::, the corpus file written by link::Classes/FluidModel#-store::.

ARGUMENT:: path
The folder.

ARGUMENT:: name
The name used when storing.

returns:: A FluidLoadStore.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: files
An Array of link::Classes/SoundFile::s (headers only) for the original files.

METHOD:: index
The index dictionary: file name -> code::(bounds: [startFrame, endFrame], numchans: ..., sr: ..., path: ...)::.

METHOD:: buffer
The joined link::Classes/Buffer::.

EXAMPLES::

code::
// after ~model.store(path) and ~model.load(path), see FluidModel
~model.loader;                         // a FluidLoadStore
~model.loader.files.collect(_.path);   // the original sound files
~model.loader.index.keysValuesDo { |name, entry| [name, entry[\bounds]].postln };

// which file and time a slice comes from
(
var info = ~model.getSlice(10);
var file = ~model.loader.files[info[4].asInteger];
var start = ~model.loader.index[file.path.basename.asSymbol][\bounds][0];
"% at % s".format(file.path.basename, (info[1] - start) / file.sampleRate).postln;
)
::
